Security: One event with endless recurrences no longer breaks the whole calendar

A single event whose recurrences exceed what Sabre expands while filtering
(for example FREQ=MINUTELY since 2000) made every time-range query of its
calendar fail with HTTP 500 (MaxInstancesExceededException). No event of that
calendar could be loaded any more, and in a calendar shared with write access
any member could make it unusable for everybody.

Such an object is now returned unfiltered - the database query has already
limited it to the requested time range - and a warning is logged. The other
events of the calendar are returned as before.
